## Grant

The translations in this repository are made available to the public for **personal, non-commercial, non-redistributable use only**, under the following terms:

### You MAY

- **Read** the translations for personal study, scholarship, or research
- **Print** copies for your own personal use
- **Quote** short passages (a single chapter, a single page, a single page image) with proper attribution to the translator
- **Reference** the translations in academic work, with citation

### You MAY NOT

- **Reproduce** the translations in whole or in substantial part for distribution
- **Publish** the translations or substantial portions in any form (print, digital, audio)
- **Sell** the translations or any derivative work based on them
- **Use** the translations for commercial purposes of any kind
- **Remove or obscure** the watermark on any rendered page (the watermark is part of the license; obscuring it is a license violation)
- **Claim authorship** of the translations; authorship remains with Shane Coy / Node Arcanum
- **Modify** the translations and present the modified version as a substitute for the original

### Attribution

When quoting or referencing, cite as:

> Shane Coy / Node Arcanum (translator), *Shams al-Ma'arif* (2026), personal-use-only translation.

## Watermark

All rendered PDF pages contain a watermark in the top-left corner:

> **@nodedotshane  ·  personal use only**

The watermark is integral to the license. Pages distributed without the watermark are not covered by this grant. If you obtain a watermark-free copy from a source other than this repository, please notify the author.

## Original source texts

The medieval Arabic source texts (al-Buni's *Shams al-Ma'arif*, the *Picatrix* / *Ghayat al-Hakim*, and other works in the Node Arcanum collection) are in the **public domain** in the United States and most jurisdictions. The original source texts are not part of this license — only the English translations and rendered PDFs in this repository are.

The Node Arcanum public repository distributes **translations and rendered PDFs only**, not the original-language manuscripts.

## Why strict?

This is the first public release of substantial translation work. Until the translations are reviewed for accuracy and the corpus matures, strict terms are appropriate. The license may be relaxed in future versions of the repo.

